  "title": "A-long Large-Cap Low-Volatility Preregistration",
  "description": "Research-only preregistration for an externally-literature-motivated single-factor low_volatility hypothesis in the reviewed A-share large-cap top-500 universe. It is NOT derived from an in-sample diagnostic of a prior run; it targets the relative-NAV drawdown axis the cash_conversion clue failed and is held to the identical frozen -0.15 gate. It freezes one low_volatility primary cell (negative trailing 252-trading-day realized volatility, percentile-ranked, marginal industry+size neutral), a two-tier verdict (statistical alpha clue vs tradeable candidate), a sub-period robustness gate, a trailing-window startup-coverage convention, and a singleton test-budget boundary. It reuses already-reviewed materialized/audited data including the full-main-board daily close series, fetches nothing, runs no signal search, authorizes no production use, and proves no alpha.",
